From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Keep internal displays visible at minimum brightness

Plasma's lowest brightness turns some built-in panels fully off.

KWinDisplayBrightness reports a safe minimum of 0, so every slider and
brightness key may ask kwin for 0.0. kwin maps that to raw level 1 of the
backlight it drives (lerp(1, max, 0.0)), and DCS-dimmed panels are black
there: the RP6's vtdr6130 sits at 4/4095 on its DSI node, the Nova
(il97680a) and Thor (ch13726a) go dark the same way.

Internal panels now report max/20 (500 of kwin's 10000) as the safe
minimum. ScreenBrightnessController clamps every write to it, so the lowest
setting lands at 5% of the backlight's range (RP6: 52/1023 on the pwm node,
208/4095 on the DSI node, lit). External displays keep 0.

The org.kde.ScreenBrightness D-Bus API subtracts the minimum, so desktop
Plasma's applet still reads 0-100%. The legacy BrightnessControl API, which
Plasma Mobile's quick-settings slider uses, passes raw values: the bottom 5%
of that slider snaps back to the floor.

Drop when upstream powerdevil reports a non-zero safe minimum for internal
kwin outputs, or kwin's own floor for internal panels keeps them lit.
---
 daemon/controllers/kwinbrightness.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/daemon/controllers/kwinbrightness.cpp b/daemon/controllers/kwinbrightness.cpp
index d3136ab..f48fb07 100644
--- a/daemon/controllers/kwinbrightness.cpp
+++ b/daemon/controllers/kwinbrightness.cpp
@@ -151,7 +151,8 @@ QString KWinDisplayBrightness::label() const

 int KWinDisplayBrightness::knownSafeMinBrightness() const
 {
-    return 0;
+    // KWin uses a 0-10,000 scale; keep handheld panels visible at 5%.
+    return isInternal() ? maxBrightness() / 20 : 0;
 }

 int KWinDisplayBrightness::maxBrightness() const
